            "title": "Incorrect handling of res.send(status, number) removed causing loss of number JSON sending behavior",
            "severity": "high",
            "file": "lib/response.js",
            "line": 105,
            "explanation": "The code previously distinguished between res.send called with a single numeric argument and res.send called with a status code and a separate number to send as JSON.\nThe removed code handled the case where res.send(status, number) would send the number as JSON. This change deletes that code resulting in calls to res.send(status, number) no longer sending the number as JSON but instead treating the first numeric argument as status and sending status text as body.\nThis is a breaking change and re",
            "suggestion": "Restore the handling for res.send(status, number) by re-adding logic that sends the numeric second argument as JSON when res.send is called with two arguments, the first a numeric status and the second a number to send."
          }
